{"kind":"request","text":"One span per judged act and per delivery, with fixed attribute names.\n\nDefine and emit one span per judged act and one per delivery attempt, with a fixed set of attribute names, so a trace of a request shows which scope judged what, at which position, with which answer.\n\nSource: Hugh's request of 28 October 2026, after a review of the alchemy Domain package, whose kernel opens a span per decision with stream, sequence, command id and correlation id, and counts commits, rejections and deliveries. The planner may fold this into the observability design (notes/2026-10-12-observability-design.md, sink and slot map) or sequence it after that design.\n\nToday: packages/scope/src/correlation.ts parses an incoming traceparent and allots a request id. There is no span per turn, no span per delivery and no agreed attribute vocabulary. The census and health routes report counts.\n\nWanted:\n1. A span `dap.act` around each turn with attributes: scope id, incarnation, definition digest, act kind, intent idempotency key, signer key id, answer, refusal reason and name, position and hash when accepted, timed rules drained, commit duration. A span `dap.delivery` per attempt: source scope and position, send ordinal, target, attempt number, result. A span `dap.read` per read: read name, `at` head, complete flag.\n2. Four counters (acts by answer, refusals by reason, deliveries by result, timed firings) and a histogram of turn duration. The names and attribute keys go in one table in the docs as the stable vocabulary.\n3. Emission through the sink the observability design chooses. On Workers the trace context propagates on sends, so a delivery's span is a child of the sending act's span.\n4. No attribute carries field values, texts or member handles: only identifiers, kinds, reasons, answers and sizes.\n5. A witness that one request through the hosted MCP endpoint yields one act span and one delivery span with the listed attributes.","body":{"conditions":"Landed on main with the vocabulary table, the spans and counters, and the hosted MCP witness; or superseded by a planner act naming the request that carries this work.","target_head":"0881c1bca1df31a9fdb4ae72947cbbedf1b3ec51","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}